content.text:
Install the official HashiCorp Terraform extension (`hashicorp.terraform`), then tell VS Code to use it for `.tf`/`.tfvars` files instead of Prettier. Add this to your VS Code `settings.json` (workspace or user):

```json
{
  "[terraform]": {
    "editor.defaultFormatter": "hashicorp.terraform",
    "editor.formatOnSave": true
  },
  "[terraform-vars]": {
    "editor.defaultFormatter": "hashicorp.terraform",
    "editor.formatOnSave": true
  }
}
```

The extension runs `terraform fmt` under the hood, so it produces canonical HCL formatting and requires `terraform` on your `PATH` (or the extension's bundled binary, depending on version).

If you have a workspace-wide Prettier override (e.g. `"editor.defaultFormatter": "esbenp.prettier-vscode"` at the top level, or a `.vscode/settings.json` in this repo already setting it globally), the language-specific `[terraform]` block above takes precedence for those file types — no need to remove the global Prettier default.

Want me to check whether this repo already has a `.vscode/settings.json` and add the override there so it's shared with the team?

